  "response_text": "If the thread function didn\u2019t loop continuously, and instead printing something and returned, the CPU would try to pop a return address from the thread\u2019s stack to continue execution. Since the thread was never meant to return and wasn\u2019t setup for this, the return address would likely be invalid or could point to some random memory. This would likely cause a hard fault, and this is why threads should have an explicit termination handler if the if it doesn\u2019t loop continuously.\\n",
